> > Question is--do I have to have my library on my person in
> > order to get a spellbook I don't have?  Do I have to have them
> > in open inventory, or can they be in a BoH?  I'm back at the
> > altar and I (now that I know create monster) am going to start
> > a sacri-fest before going on the Quest.

It only uses what spells you know not what you have in your
possession:

"The game will try (level+1) times to randomly select a spell you
do not already know (using the usual object generation algorithm),
then give you a random book. If holding a magic marker, you may
get a spellbook of blank paper. The book is always blessed."

This means you could read a book, dip it blank, then never see
that type of book again.  I have no idea if amensia or mind
flayer forgetfullness counts against what books you know.

Notice that it only tries XP+1 times.  Players who avoid leveling
up are less likely to see good variety in spellbooks while players
at XP=30 can end up seeing excellent variety.  (I have tried
altar camping with an XP=30 Valkyrie and she got all sorts of
spellbooks in the process of building up her AC).

> No, it would only have had mattered if you had a spellbook of
> restory ability in your inventory when you were crowned (well, I
> think so). If you want to minimize the chance for blank spellbooks
> identify them soon (by reading) and don't carry a magic marker.

It cares if you know a type of book.  Reading a blank book
identifies it.  Else you may build up blessed blank books.



